othing and say what remains blocked. Then, unless the user asked for a specific change, decide where it belongs, by this session's environment. If `is_default` is true, all the user's repositories use it, so what only one repository needs stays off it: move this session to an environment in `saved_for_session_repositories` with switch_environment and call this tool again (if none is `switchable_by_you`, propose nothing and tell the user which is saved for this repository and why this session cannot move to it), or, if the list is empty, propose a personal one with create_environment and `switch_session`. Edit the Default when every project would want the change, `session_has_repository` is false, or the list is empty and `switch_session` is not offered. A repo's setup script is never for the Default. In any other environment, edit when `editable_by_you` is true, whichever repository it was made for; otherwise propose a personal environment with create_environment, or tell the user the `not_editable_reason`. request_credential saves on the environment this session runs in. (5) Propose once and say why, with the evidence. If the user declines, do not propose a change for that need again in this session.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"environment_id": {"description": "The environment ID to look up (starts with 'env_'), e.g. from list_environments. Omit to look up the environment this session is running in.", "type": "string"}}, "required": [], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__get_environment"}, "server": "claude-code-remote"}, {"description": "Fetch a single transcript event from a Claude Code Remote session by session_id and event_uuid. Returns the event's role, content, isSynthetic, and inbound_origin. Same authorization as list_events.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__get_event", "schema": {"description": "Fetch a single transcript event from a Claude Code Remote session by session_id and event_uuid. Returns 